      "url": "https://x.com/spacetimedb/status/2029910947779739728",
      "created_at": "2026-03-06T13:24:18+00:00",
      "text": "Horizontal scaling is always possible.",
      "lang": "en",
      "like_count": 1,
      "retweet_count": 0,
      "reply_count": 1,
      "impression_count": 501
    },
    {
      "id": "2029910452671574335",
      "url": "https://x.com/spacetimedb/status/2029910452671574335",
      "created_at": "2026-03-06T13:22:20+00:00",
      "text": "People often over index into horizontal scaling over vertical scaling because of theoretical limitations of vertical scaling. The truth is you need both, but vertical scaling should always come first.\n\n100,000 tx/s on a single core is strictly better than 1,000 tx/s on 100 cores.",
      "lang": "en",
      "like_count": 39,
      "retweet_count": 1,
      "reply_count": 5,
      "impression_count": 3631
    },
